## Summary

**SEC18 — local anti-phishing/malware domain blocklist** ("poor-man's Safe Browsing", zero lookups):

- **Rust core** (`src/rustcore/src/blocklist.rs`): memory-safe matcher, `rc_blocklist_check/load/reload/count` FFI. Exact + parent-suffix matching on label boundaries; IP literals exact-match only; parses URLhaus hostfile rows, OpenPhish URL rows, and adblock-style entries. Active set = vendored seed ∪ data-dir override, so a poisoned download can never shrink coverage.
- **Qt updater** (`src/network/domainblocklist.*`): fetches URLhaus + OpenPhish through the existing consent-gated HTTPS adblock-list path (weekly cadence, atomic write, reload).
- **Interceptors**: privacy + tor interceptors refuse listed main-frame navigations before strip/upgrade stages, recording the refusal consume-once.
- **Interstitial**: nonce-bound `arora-site-block:` warning page naming the domain — "Back to safety" plus a session-only, logged "Proceed anyway". Deliberately no persisted bypass.
- **Toggle**: `privacy/domainBlocklist` (default on); no-rust builds fully inert.

**Verified**: `cargo test` 19/19; `tst_domainblock` 13/13 under `CONFIG+=rustcore` (fixture block, suffix/lookalike matching, real interstitial render + click-through, forged-nonce rejection, redirect/subframe semantics, consent gate, loopback update round-trip) and 13/13 no-rust; check-warnings PASS; `make check` 62 programs 0 failed offscreen with `--disable-gpu`.

One wrinkle worth noting: `CONFIG+=rustcore` doesn't propagate to stale subdir Makefiles (known SEC17 issue), so flagged objects were rebuilt via per-dir qmake + forced `.o` rebuilds, then restored to default before the suite run.
